{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared INPUT vectors for the canonical-JSON parity proof. Transport only:",
    "scripts/verify-hash-parity.mjs parses this file in JavaScript, scripts/canonical-cli.py",
    "parses it in Python, and both must serialise every vector to identical bytes.",
    "",
    "Numbers here MUST be written as plain integer literals. A form like 1e2 or 1.0 would",
    "parse to the integer 100 in JavaScript and the float 100.0 in Python, so the two",
    "languages would disagree about whether the vector is even legal. The loader rejects",
    "those spellings so the hazard cannot be reintroduced silently.",
    "",
    "Strings use \\u escapes rather than literal bytes so this file stays pure ASCII and",
    "cannot be mangled by an editor normalising Unicode."
  ],
